          "description": {
            "comment": "Syntroaceticus schinkii is a mesophilic strict anaerobic bacterium oxidizing acetate to CO2 and H2 in syntrophic association with a methanogenic partner. The methanogenic partner in this peculiar syntrophic relationship finally produces methane. S. schinkii can also grow as heterotroph without the methanogenic partner.The key enzymes of this homoacetatic fermentation (Wood-Ljungdahl pathway) are suggested to be used both during syntrophic acetate oxidation as well as acetate formation. The proposed reversibility of this pathway is of specific interest since syntrophic acetate oxidation operates close to the energetic limitations of microbial life.",
